**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** A dial-mounted item is scanned by its raw dial reading (001 §I 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (`DialSign` exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; 001 §K 'dial 0…360 step 20'; the S8.2 mapper's request: dial scans record readings). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `VariableParameter` (`Experiments.fs:VariableParameter`) gains `VaryDialReading` after `VaryR2`, with `code` `dial`, `label` `Dial reading` and `unitLabel` `°`; `allowedFor` is unchanged, because a kind does not know its item's mounting; `VariableRange.forVariable VaryDialReading` is 0…360° over 19 points. Every match over the variable gains the case, no wildcard arm hiding it (FS0025): `MeasuredData.validateAgainstExperiment` treats it as `VaryR1` (no wavelength check), `OutOfBandDiagnostic.requestedWavelengthsFor` as a fixed wavelength, and the host's arms below. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`, after step 277's members: `type SetupSlot with member this.scanVariablesWith (items : Item list) : VariableParameter list` is `VariableParameter.allowedFor` of the slot's `placement.catalogueKind` with `VaryR1` replaced by `VaryDialReading` when the slot holds (`content.itemOpt`, step 256) an item of `items` whose `dial` is `DialMounted _` (step 215): the angle of such an item is a reading, and the table records readings (step 258's `recordedWith`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`: the domain-free mirror `VariableChoice` (`ExperimentControls.fs:VariableChoice`) gains `VaryDialReading`, `uiKey` `dial` and `caption` `Dial reading`, and `allVariables` (`ExperimentControls.fs:allVariables`) lists it last, so the bay draws its box under `ConstructorUiId.experimentVariable`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the domain ⇄ Controls mirror maps gain the case; `ExpChooseElement` and the bay's `variableChoices` read `slot.scanVariablesWith model.kitItems` where they read `VariableParameter.allowedFor`; and `chartForRun` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`) sweeps a `VaryDialReading` of the varied slot as it sweeps `VaryR1`, each swept reading x evaluated at the physical angle `sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle (Angle.degree x)` of the slot's item (steps 255, 258), with `xLabel` `Dial reading (°)`, the vary text `the dial reading over <lo>…<hi>°`, the title `<quantity> vs dial reading` and `AngularXAxis`; a slot whose item is not dial-mounted is never offered the variable. No other variable, option or conversion is added. Tests. `SetupTests` gains `a dial-mounted item's slot scans its dial reading where a fixed one scans R1`: over its `lpA` slot and step 277's items, holding `LP1` (fixed) it scans `[ VaryR1 ]`, holding a test-local `LPd` (`DialMounted DialNegative`, `dialZero` known at 10°) `[ VaryDialReading ]`, and `sampleA` holding `QZd` scans `[ VaryDialReading; VaryR2 ]`; and `VariableRange.forVariable VaryDialReading` sweeps 0, 20, …, 360. `ExperimentControlsTests` (ui-tests) gains `a dial scan draws the run at the physical angle of each reading`: over a table whose analyzer slot holds `LPd` behind a linear polarizer, choosing it offers the `dial` box and no `r1` box, and the draft's chart over readings 0…360° (19 points) equals, point for point within 1e-12, the chart of the same table with a fixed analyzer varied in R1 over the physical angles `DialNegative.physicalAngleOf 10° x`, its x values being the readings. Every other fact passes as written; `ElementMenuTests`, `FsxAcceptanceTests`, `InverseConstructorTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` name `VariableChoice` cases and compile as they are, nothing in them changing.

**Acceptance.** After the dial reading lands, `VariableParameter.VaryDialReading` MUST be offered for a slot holding a dial-mounted item in place of R1 (`SetupSlot.scanVariablesWith`), its default range MUST be 0-360° in steps of 20, and chartForRun MUST evaluate each reading at its physical angle; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a dial-mounted item's slot scans its dial reading where a fixed one scans R1`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a dial scan draws the run at the physical angle of each reading`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
